    "result_text": "The build is green. The full test suite runs and passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement in the owner create pipeline (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), the single endpoint (`POST /api/owners`) that creates owners.\n\nChanges:\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger.\n2. **Added `enqueueWelcomeNotification(Owner)`**, which emits one line via the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner id and the memberId: `\"Welcome owner id={} memberId={}\"`.\n3. **Wired it into `createOwner`** \u2014 called on the successful-create path only, right after `saveOwner` (so the owner id is assigned) and the existing audit emission. A gate that trips (400/409/429) short-circuits before this point, so no notification is enqueued on failure.\n\nThis mirrors the existing audit pattern, keeping the notification concern isolated in one place. The acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and the memberId read back from `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
